% A predicate the program references and nothing defines is a typo far more
% often than an intentionally empty relation.  It is reported once, at the
% first place the program names it, however many times it is referenced --
% including from a query, whose atoms are resolved like any other.
edge(a, b).

reachable(X, Y) :-
    edge(X, Y),
    not excluded(X),
    not excluded(Y).

missing(X)?
